cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Jacquard - Deterministic evidence checking for AI-assisted knowledge synthesis."
message: >-
  If you use Jacquard, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Riccardo
    family-names: Boero
    email: ribo@nilu.no
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7468-9096"
    affiliation: NILU
repository-code: "https://github.com/open-and-sustainable/jacquard"
url: "https://open-and-sustainable.github.io/jacquard/"
abstract: >-
  Jacquard is open science software for deterministic evidence checking in
  AI-assisted knowledge synthesis. It provides contracts for checking
  extracted claims against source documents, covering output structure, quote
  fidelity, text and numeric support, evidence reporting, and size-based filter
  audits. Its Go library, command-line tool, and C shared library validate JSON
  requests and reports using explicit rules and arbitrary-precision numbers.
keywords:
  - AI-assisted knowledge synthesis
  - Knowledge synthesis
  - Evidence synthesis
  - Deterministic validation
  - Information extraction
  - Validation
  - Open Source
  - Open Science
